# The upstream compile tests that cannot pass on Linux (OpenSpec change m7-linux, design D6): <category>/<name><TAB>
# <reason>, as tests/verification/known.list. A reason that starts with "windows" skips the program there; any other
# makes its failure known. Read by tools/legacy_tests/run_legacy_tests.py --platform linux. Each line was measured with
# QB64pe's Linux build too. On Windows these programs print the expected values in an $IF WINDOWS branch.
audio_sound_test/sound_test	varies: crashes now and then in libqb's audio engine with no sound device (munmap_chunk or a segfault, as v29_a_sound_queue): 1 of 40 runs 8 at a time on 2026-11-06, QB64pe's Linux build 7 of 40; upstream's 50c371e13 (pull request 800) makes the audio engine thread-safe
